{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>Rejoice, O nations, with His people.</b> At that time the nations will praise Israel — they will see the praiseworthiness of this nation, that they clung to the Holy One, blessed be He, through all the troubles that passed over them and did not abandon Him; they knew His goodness and His praise." "<b>For the blood of His servants He will avenge.</b> The shedding of their blood — as its meaning." "<b>And vengeance He will repay to His adversaries.</b> For the robbery and the violence, as the matter that is stated (Joel 4): ״Egypt shall be a desolation and Edom shall be a desolate wilderness, for the violence against the children of Judah,״ and it says (Obadiah 10): ״For the violence against your brother Jacob, etc.״ (see Sifrei)." "<b>And He will atone His land, His people.</b> And He will appease His land and His people for the troubles that passed over them and that the enemy did to them." "<b>And He will atone.</b> A term of appeasement and conciliation, as in (Genesis 32:21) ״I will appease his face״ — אַנְחִינֵיהּ לְרוּגְזֵיהּ." "<b>And He shall atone His land.</b> And what is 'His land'? <b>His people.</b> When His people are comforted, His land is comforted. And so it says, ״You forgave, YHWH, Your land״ — in what did You forgive Your land? ״You restored the fortune of Jacob״ (Psalms 85)." "It is expounded in another manner in Sifrei, and Rabbi Yehudah and Rabbi Nechemiah disagreed on it. Rabbi Yehudah expounds all of it concerning Israel, and Rabbi Nechemyah expounds all of it concerning the nations. Rabbi Yehudah expounds it concerning Israel — (26) <b>I said, I would scatter them</b> as I explained, through (27) <b>Were it not that the wrath of the enemy had been held back.</b> (28) <b>For they are a nation void of counsel.</b> They lost My Torah, which is sound counsel for them, <b>and there is no understanding in them</b> to consider. (30) <b>How should one pursue</b> from the nations <b>a thousand</b> of them — <b>were it not that their Rock had sold them.</b> (31) <b>For their rock is not like our Rock.</b> All as I explained through to the end. And Rabbi Nechemyah expounds it concerning the nations — <b>For they are a nation void of counsel</b>, as I explained at the beginning, through <b>and their judges consider.</b>" "(32) <b>For their vine is from the vine of Sodom.</b> Of the nations." "<b>And from the fields of Gomorrah…</b> They do not set their heart to ascribe greatness to Me." "<b>Their grapes are grapes of rosh.</b> This is what it says — <b>Were it not for the wrath of the enemy I would gather</b> upon Israel, to poison them and embitter them. Therefore <b>their clusters are bitter to them</b> — to feed them for what they did to My children." "<b>Their venom is the venom of serpents.</b> Prepared to make them drink it, because of what they do to them." "<b>Like the draining of its dregs.</b> That cup, about which it is said (Psalms 75) ״כִּי כוֹס בְּיַד ה'״ וגו׳." "<b>When their foot slips.</b> As in that which is said ״תִּרְמְסֶנָּה רֶגֶל״ (Isaiah 26)." "<b>For YHWH will judge His people.</b> In this expression <b>כי ידין</b> functions in the sense of הִנֵּה — and יָדִין is not a term of suffering but rather like ״He will plead their cause״ from the hand of their oppressors. <b>For He will see that their power is gone, etc.</b>" "<b>And he will say: Where are their gods?</b> The enemy will say: Where is the Elohim of Israel? As the wicked Titus said when he pierced the curtain (Gittin 56), as in that which is said (Micah 7): ״וְתֵרֶא אֹיַבְתִּי וּתְכַסֶּהָ בוּשָׁה הָאוֹמְרָה אֵלַי אַיּוֹ ה' אֱלֹהָיִךְ״." "<b>See now that I, etc.</b> Then the Holy One, blessed be He, will reveal His salvation and say: <b>See now that I, I am He</b> — from Me comes the evil upon them, and from Me will come the good upon them." "<b>And none delivers.</b> Who would deliver you from the evil that I bring upon you." "<b>For I lift up to heaven My hand.</b> Like כִּי נָשָׂאתִי — I always cause My Shekhinah to dwell in heaven, as the Targum renders. Even if weak above and strong below, the dread of the Supreme is upon the nether — all the more so when strong above and weak below." "<b>My hand.</b> The place of My Shekhinah, as in ״אִישׁ עַל יָדוֹ״ (Numbers 2). And it was in My power to take vengeance on you, but I said that I live forever — I do not hasten to punish, for I have delay in the matter. I live forever, and in later generations I exact punishment from them, and the power is in My hand to punish both the dead and the living. A king of flesh and blood who is going to death hastens his vengeance to exact it in his lifetime — for perhaps he or his enemy will die, and it turns out that he did not see his vengeance against him. But I live forever, and if they die and I do not punish them in their lifetime, I will punish them in their death." "<b>If I sharpen the flash of My sword.</b> Many times there are verses that are not suspended — when I vocalize <b>the flash of My sword and My hand grasps judgment</b>, all of it is as I explained above."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {4 "אַנְחִינֵיהּ לְרוּגְזֵיהּ is Aramaic: 'I will calm His anger' — Onkelos's rendering of Genesis 32:21."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:51.798383620Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}